{
  "name": "Crazy Quilt",
  "aliases": ["Indian Carpet", "Japanese Rug"],
  "description": "**Goal:** build all eight foundations to move every card home — four built **up in suit from Ace to King**, four built **down in suit from King to Ace** (two decks, so each suit fills one up-pile and one down-pile).\n\n- The foundations **start seeded** with an Ace and a King of each suit.\n- The **quilt** is 64 cards woven in a lattice. A quilt card is **available** when **either of its short ends** is clear — i.e. one of the two neighbours it points at is gone (cards on the rim start free).\n- Play any available quilt card, or the **waste** top, onto a foundation.\n- You may also lay an available quilt card on the **waste** if it is one rank **up or down** (any suit, and Ace/King wrap) — this chains, and is the main way to dig the weave open. Waste cards then only advance to foundations.\n- Draw from the **stock** to the waste; you may recycle the waste **once per game** when the stock runs out.",
  "decks": [{ "count": 2 }],
